Trademarks and distribution identity
------------------------------------

The MIT License grants rights to the software, not to names, logos, or infrastructure.

- "DeepSeek" and "DeepSeek Harness" are trademarks of their respective owner. This project is an
  unofficial community build. It must not be presented as an official DeepSeek release.
- The upstream application uses the identifier `com.deepseek.dsh` and the update feed
  `harness.deepseek.com`. A community build must not reuse either: an official app ID would make
  the package indistinguishable from a release build, and the official update feed would deliver
  Windows and macOS updates to a Linux installation.
- Any redistributed package must state that it is unofficial in its package description, its
  `.desktop` entry, and its documentation.

Model usage is separate from the application license
----------------------------------------------------

This application being free and open source does not make model inference free. Running an agent
session requires a DeepSeek account and API access, which have their own terms and pricing.
